window.QB_MATHS_QBTEST3 = {"subject":"DP Mathematics: Analysis and Approaches","level":"SL","topic":{"number":4,"title":"Statistics and probability"},"exercises":[{"id":"17N.1.SL.TZ0.T_1","section":"A","paper":1,"session":"17N","date":"November 2017","tz":"TZ0","legacy":"T_","marks":4,"contexts":[{"id":"c1","html":"<p>A group of 20 students travelled to a gymnastics tournament together. Their ages, in years, are given in the following table.</p><p><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\"></p><p>The lower quartile of the ages is 16 and the upper quartile is 18.5.</p>"}],"parts":[{"label":"a.ii","type":"question","marks":1,"ctx":["c1"],"q":"<p>For the students in this group write down the median age.</p>","ms":"<p>16.5&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<em><strong>(A1)(C1)</strong></em></p>","er":""},{"label":"b","type":"question","marks":3,"ctx":["c1"],"q":"<p>Draw a box-and-whisker diagram, for these students’ ages, on the following grid.</p><p><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\"></p>","ms":"<p><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\"></p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<em><strong>(A1)(A1)(A1)(ft)(C3)</strong></em></p><p><strong>Note:</strong> Award (A1) for correct endpoints, (A1) for correct quartiles, (A1)(ft) for their median. Follow through from part (a)(ii), but only if median is between 16 and 18.5. If a horizontal line goes through the box, award at most (A1)(A1)(A0). Award at most (A0)(A1)(A1) if a ruler has not been used.</p>","er":""}],"notes":[]},{"id":"16N.1.SL.TZ0.T_2","section":"A","paper":1,"session":"16N","date":"November 2016","tz":"TZ0","legacy":"T_","marks":3,"contexts":[{"id":"c1","html":"<p>A sample of 120 oranges was tested for Vitamin C content. The cumulative frequency curve below represents the Vitamin C content, in milligrams, of these oranges.</p><p><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\"></p><p>The minimum level of Vitamin C content of an orange in the sample was 30.1 milligrams. The maximum level of Vitamin C content of an orange in the sample was 35.0 milligrams.</p>"}],"parts":[{"label":"","type":"question","marks":3,"ctx":["c1"],"q":"<p>Draw a box-and-whisker diagram on the grid below to represent the Vitamin C content, in milligrams, for this sample.</p><p><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\"></p>","ms":"<p><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\"></p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<em><strong>(A1)(ft)(A1)(ft)(A1)</strong></em></p><p><strong>Note:</strong> Award (A1)(ft) for correct median, (A1)(ft) for correct quartiles and box, (A1) for correct end points of whiskers and straight whiskers. Award at most (A1)(A1)(A0) if a horizontal line goes right through the box or if the whiskers are not well aligned with the midpoint of the box. Follow through from part (a).</p>","er":""}],"notes":[]},{"id":"17M.1.SL.TZ2.S_8","section":"A","paper":1,"session":"17M","date":"May 2017","tz":"TZ2","legacy":"S_","marks":2,"contexts":[{"id":"c1","html":"<p>A city hired 160 employees to work at a festival. The following cumulative frequency curve shows the number of hours employees worked during the festival.</p><p><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\"></p><p>The city paid each of the employees £8 per hour for the first 40 hours worked, and £10 per hour for each hour they worked after the first 40 hours.</p>"}],"parts":[{"label":"a.ii","type":"question","marks":1,"ctx":["c1"],"q":"<p>Write down the number of employees who worked 50 hours or less.</p>","ms":"<p>130 employees&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<em><strong>A1 N1</strong></em></p>","er":""},{"label":"b.i","type":"question","marks":1,"ctx":["c1"],"q":"<p>Find the amount of money an employee earned for working 40 hours.</p>","ms":"<p>£320&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<em><strong>A1 N1</strong></em></p>","er":""}],"notes":[]},{"id":"EXN.1.SL.TZ0.4","section":"A","paper":1,"session":"EXN","date":"November Example questions","tz":"TZ0","legacy":"","marks":7,"contexts":[{"id":"c1","html":"<p>A food scientist measures the weights of 760 potatoes taken from a single field and the distribution of the weights is shown by the cumulative frequency curve below.</p><p><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\"></p>"},{"id":"c2","html":"<p>The weight of the smallest potato in the sample is 20 grams and the weight of the largest is 400 grams.</p>"}],"parts":[{"label":"a","type":"question","marks":2,"ctx":["c1"],"q":"<p>Find the number of potatoes in the sample with a weight of more than 200 grams.</p>","ms":"<p>760 − 420 = 340 (g)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<em><strong>(M1)A1</strong></em></p>","er":""},{"label":"b.i","type":"question","marks":1,"ctx":["c1"],"q":"<p>Find the median weight.</p>","ms":"<p>Median = 190 (g)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<em><strong>A1</strong></em></p>","er":""},{"label":"b.ii","type":"question","marks":1,"ctx":["c1"],"q":"<p>Find the lower quartile.</p>","ms":"<p>Lower quartile = 135 − 140 (g)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<em><strong>A1</strong></em></p>","er":""},{"label":"b.iii","type":"question","marks":1,"ctx":["c1"],"q":"<p>Find the upper quartile.</p>","ms":"<p>Upper quartile = 242 − 247 (g)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<em><strong>A1</strong></em></p>","er":""},{"label":"c","type":"question","marks":2,"ctx":["c1","c2"],"q":"<p>Use the scale shown below to draw a box and whisker diagram showing the distribution of the weights of the potatoes. You may assume there are no outliers.</p><p><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\"></p>","ms":"<p><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\"></p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<em><strong>M1A1</strong></em></p><p><strong>Note:</strong> The M1 is for a box and whisker plot and the A1 for all 5 statistics in the right places.</p>","er":""}],"notes":[]}]};
